{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1248937-v5-vienna-tremere-friends","id":1248937,"title":"V5 Vienna, Tremere & friends","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-26T04:15:11-07:00","id":1248937,"title":"V5 Vienna, Tremere & friends","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> After BJD I am pretty curious about the Saulot/Tremere drama, so one thing I was waiting for in V5 was for the continuation of the story. I've made my own things for my games, so I'm not planning on following it, but if any one knows some new content about the TS drama I would love to read it!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16128-kalendeer","name":"Kalendeer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T05:35:31-07:00","id":1248941,"title":"","content":"We don\u2019t know anything about the top level yet, but we do know a few ground-level things:<br /> <br /> 1) the Vienna chantry was destroyed by the 2nd Inquisition in what is probably their biggest raid to date. If you\u2019re wondering how they got into such a well magicked stronghold, technology notwithstanding, then you\u2019re thinking correctly. Somebody up the chain had to let them. Possibly Saulot, or possibly Tremere or Carna trying to get st the Saulot-controlled portion of the clan. <br /> <br /> 2) the rupture if the pyramid and the Council of Seven has caused the Tremere blood to reject the clan bond, leading to the possibility of splinter houses. Carna\u2019s faction has split into its own house within the clan. Goratrix is still kicking around and has his own house again. Most of the clan still think of themselves as House Tremere and firmly within the Camarilla, but there are options now, as the clan is no longer monolithic. More trilithic. But the houses are in dialog with each other and not necessarily antagonistic. They just no longer have a central authority and thus have different standards for initiates and can operate independently. <br /> <br /> 3) it\u2019s not clear the degree to which the main House Tremere is still actively Saulot-controlled, but if it is, his power has been reduced. That\u2019s good for both Goratrix (the real Tremere) and Carna, who now have more freedom to operate. Overall the clan has moved to training and working in smaller groups, with the master/sire-apprentice relationship being key. It\u2019s also true that some young Tremere have to pursue their studies on their own, hunting down texts and such because there isn\u2019t some big university-chantey with all the stuff already there. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s possible I\u2019ve missed some illuminating flavor text here and there, but that\u2019s the lion\u2019s share of what we know. I look forward to seeing if there are Anarch Tremere now. Lots of folks assume House Carna has gone officially Anarch, but she denies that\u2019s the case. I imagine her flight to the Free States in BJD was a matter of survival as much as anything. Also not clear on the degree to which Goratrix is now operating apart from the Sabbat, possibly going Anarch himself now that the Sabbat is a mess (again). The question is where he can most effectively battle an Antediluvian for control of his clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T08:14:41-07:00","id":1248960,"title":"","content":"I hope Etrius is not dead, because he was my favorite NPC in the lore (yes I have strange tastes, he just checks all my boxes by having messed up Faith, being an hypocrite, self-righteous, authoritarian, power crazy AND submissive).<br /> <br /> In my games Goratrix/Tremere allegieance will depend on the actions of a PC elder coterie who sway him to any faction, but my default idea would be that he would go autarkis Giovanni-style, because the Camarilla Tremere were Etrius and Meerlinda first while he was alseep, he is not really Goratrix, and definitly not an anarch. So now that Tremere is free, I am not sure he would fit anywhere.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I would love to have Carna's house as an &quot;anarch&quot; house with a more egalitarian approach to thauma... as long as you belong to the House. They would also enlist kindred from other clans and swear them in with Vaulderie-like rituals to serve the House, only the House would be a collectivist whole instead of a pyramid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16128-kalendeer","name":"Kalendeer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T09:04:39-07:00","id":1249431,"title":"","content":"Must admit that the whole &quot;House Carna&quot; thing got me by surprise and i utterly love it because Carna as i remember her from Milwaulkee by Night is an utterly horrible, terrible choice of a person to become a sort of leader among the Tremere, what to say the head and founder of a splinter house. such a lovely, bloody mess. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On the matter of Etrius i'm kind of divided because i remember how he was described back in Children of Inquisition and it's hard not to see that, entertaining though it may be, his characterization was atrociously flanderized and messed up from VtDA onwards to the point of becoming pretty much a whole different person.<br /> <br /> That along with the fact i had toyed with my own alternate takes of clan Tremere origins back in 1e before we got the tale of the Salubri and Saulot.... and well, let's say my relation with Etrius and the Tremere's founding can be, conflicted. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T10:57:39-07:00","id":1249490,"title":"","content":"My personal take is that either Saulot got the 2nd Inq to reduce the Clan and headquarters in an attempt to retake control. <br /> <br /> Carna Im thinking might be the Tzimisce influence, or in league with Master of Ravens, should that still be a thing, both because it feels like the V5 version of the Fire Flower and like a neo-Koldunish thing. <br /> <br /> Honestly, House Carna I care least about, but Im not too sure we will be getting any real answers to things. Carna could very easily be Tremere's","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 08-28-2018, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T16:09:42-07:00","id":1249558,"title":"","content":"My theory is Tremere is behind the Vienna chantry being destroyed. He eliminated Saulot potential control of his clan (not sure if this was really the case but better safe then sorry). No doubt that Tremere is behind house Goratrix. Its hinted that the three houses are somehow mystically compelled to, if not work together, at least avoid out right civil war. No doubt Carna would have been attacked by now otherwise. Most likely this is how Tremere intends things to be.<br /> <br /> I strongly doubt Carna is under Tzimisce or anyone elses influence. Turns out shes not so incompetent a leader or sorcerer. Carna apparently lives in fear of Tremere seeking revenge for her breaking free from the pyramid but I doubt thats the case. Most likely she has his approval though Carna is not going to be told that. Fear is a useful tool.<br /> <br /> It seems Tremere is back in control of his clan and hes doing it from the shadows. But thats just my assumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","user":"Wissenschaft","date":". 08-28-2018, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T02:13:28-07:00","id":1249649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1248937-v5-vienna-tremere-friends?p=1249431#post1249431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the matter of Etrius i'm kind of divided because i remember how he was described back in Children of Inquisition and it's hard not to see that, entertaining though it may be, his characterization was atrociously flanderized and messed up from VtDA onwards to the point of becoming pretty much a whole different person.<br /> <br /> That along with the fact i had toyed with my own alternate takes of clan Tremere origins back in 1e before we got the tale of the Salubri and Saulot.... and well, let's say my relation with Etrius and the Tremere's founding can be, conflicted. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I got the feeling that Etrius turned into a far more nefarious character in later edition than he used to be (let us all forget the Etrius from 1995 House of Secrets who is everyone high humanity sweet heart because honestly he was horribly written, one would wonder if HE was not the one to eat Saulot). While I like some things they changed from Children of the Inquisition (like his very early life story), I feel like they went a bit too far, from high humanity depressed Etrius to &quot;DEMONS! DIABLERIE! EVIL CACKLES!&quot;<br /> <br /> My Etrius would be somewhere in between, so no infernalism, and a fair amount of grooming and Dominate from Tremere to push his loyal servant through the most disgusting times of House Tremere. One of our Elder PC actually confronted him once about the Diablerie of Saulot, and oddly the version she got from Etrius (willing, quiet and smiling Saulot) was utterly inconsistent with the version she got from Saulot himself when she met him (apprently there was a fight, Tremere acted with deliberate cruaulty, and Etrius actually protested, though he does not remember it).<br /> <br /> Once Tremere sank deeper into Torpor, once Goratrix left, and when Etrius started to believe that Saulot had planned that all along to take control of the House (spoiler: he did not, but once he was here? Why not), things got better because he could do things his way and the diablerie of Saulot was still a problem, but he felt less guilty about it. I mean, it was a plot from Saulot, right? If so, Etrius is more of a victim and less of a murderer, and the Salubri and the Tremere are both preys to the same ancient evil. The hunt for the Salubri became such an half assed thing that it basically stopped. He would just conviently forget to investigate rumors of salubri, and when he got real intel about elders resting places, he whipped the memories of those involved and let them rest. He involved himself in things like creating the Camarilla and quite happily used external pressure to clean some of the mess he attributes to Goratrix (&quot;Gargoyles? Nah we don't need those... weird torture rituals? Do we need those, guys, with the Auspex and Dominate we have?&quot;).<br /> <br /> Like most Elders he is fucked up in his head due to the coping mecanism he developped to get through the worst times, Tremere's conditionning, his age and his own flaws, but he is not the cackling bad guy who laughs while diablerizing other vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16128-kalendeer","name":"Kalendeer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T02:51:23-07:00","id":1249653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1248937-v5-vienna-tremere-friends?p=1248941#post1248941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> the rupture of the pyramid and the Council of Seven has caused the Tremere blood to reject the clan bond, leading to the possibility of splinter houses.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a possibility. But it could also be a simple case of tit for tat...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T22:11:27-07:00","id":1249883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1248937-v5-vienna-tremere-friends?p=1249653#post1249653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a possibility. But it could also be a simple case of tit for tat...</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that there was a ritual they had to keep the blood from all members of Tremere and suppress whatever actual weakness the clan had before they started blood bonding the Clan (See Dark Ages 20) And it broke when Vienna was destroyed, this leaves the clan with a previous weakness or modified weakness (Depending on if you want the V20 DA Flaw to be Cannon) still to do with the blood and Blood Bonds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T22:20:10-07:00","id":1249886,"title":"","content":"Did they even have a weakness? If they were all Caitiff, perhaps in truth they have none.<br /> <br /> I wonder if their weakness wouldn't be that the Tremere actually have only two in-clans (Auspex and Dominate), Thaumaturgy being not a discipline but something they learn easily due to social conditionning rather than the blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16128-kalendeer","name":"Kalendeer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T01:03:51-07:00","id":1249899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kalendeer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1248937-v5-vienna-tremere-friends?p=1249886#post1249886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did they even have a weakness? If they were all Caitiff, perhaps in truth they have none.<br /> I wonder if their weakness wouldn't be that the Tremere actually have only two in-clans (Auspex and Dominate), Thaumaturgy being not a discipline but something they learn easily due to social conditionning rather than the blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark ages V20 gave them each draft of blood counting as 2 for blood bonding.<br /> <br /> Technically, most were embraced as Tzimesce before the &quot;Clan&quot; was created<br /> <br /> I like the idea of giving them 2 disciplines, but you'd have to change to cost for buying Thaum,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T03:39:32-07:00","id":1249919,"title":"","content":"Unless you give the same cost for Thauma for characters who are in the House but not of the blood. While it is usually not relevant, in my full-Tremere game one of the character was actually not of Tremere blood and got the same cost for buying Thauma because she was still educated as a Tremere. The in-game justification being that Tremere require less xp for their primary path not because of their blood, but because their whole vampiric education is about Thauma, while some random Anarch will, perhaps, not have the right set of mind.<br /> <br /> Remember that secondary paths cost the same for everyone, so paying out of clan cost for the primary path is still pretty much inexpensive once you start opening secondary paths. I currently have an Old Clan Tzimisce technomancer and decided to give him the path of the Levinbolt and it's ridiculously not expensive IMO.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16128-kalendeer","name":"Kalendeer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T06:12:24-07:00","id":1250236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1248937-v5-vienna-tremere-friends?p=1249883#post1249883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that there was a ritual they had to keep the blood from all members of Tremere and suppress whatever actual weakness the clan had before they started blood bonding the Clan (See Dark Ages 20) And it broke when Vienna was destroyed, this leaves the clan with a previous weakness or modified weakness (Depending on if you want the V20 DA Flaw to be Cannon) still to do with the blood and Blood Bonds.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I was referring to was to an X-factor: An outside player that could have been responsible for the Tremere's current troubles due to the clan weakness they now possess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2582,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","user":"Gangrel44","date":". 08-31-2018, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T13:24:33-07:00","id":1401180,"title":"","content":"I would be curious for more to read about too because the true love from one of the Mages in my chronic is a jewish generation 7 tremere that whas embraced during the Reichskristallnacht and survived 2008 because of her own haven outside of the chantry. She is a natural talent that managed despite her young age to reach already magister during her short unlive because she is only interested in Thaumaturgy and has an honest attitude about helping others to reach new heights there. She has been extrem loyal to the clan during the 70 years because they saved her live and where her new family but now her priorities shifted in wanting more to spend time with her boyfriend but being unclear about what to do about the situation with the clan.<br /> <br /> Right now I handled it, that the rest of the clan of the clan has no idea of her survival and she has no idea how to contact the rest because she do not know who survived and being afraid to contact any other clan members because that would mayby endagers her or them.<br /> <br /> So has anyone an advice what I should do about the three houses situation with her and where she would fit best?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 07-05-2020, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T17:18:16-07:00","id":1401226,"title":"","content":"One other theory about the Fall of Vienna and the inside job is that it was orchestrated by Karl Schreckt, who talked about issues with the SauloTremere worm and the control it had with the Council of Seven. And Schrekt was high up enough to know some of the ins and outs of everything.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26160\" data-vbnamecard=\"26160\">Koronus</a> <br /> If she's that dedicated to Thaumaturgy itself, it's possible she actually jumped Anarch and went with the Ipsissimus. What we know about them fits her 'driven by Thaumaturgical development' and 'helping others'. The Ipsissimus Tremere are all about experimentation and advancement of magic in ways that were stifled by the Tremere hierarchy and methodology, and about doing it in tandem with each other. One of the quotes from the Ipsissimus in the Anarch book is We can all achieve enlightenment, but no-one should make that journey alone. It fits her concept probably the best, since Carna is about more specific neo-pagan witchcraft styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T23:47:22-07:00","id":1401286,"title":"","content":"I think it only makes sense if it were an inside job. I dig the idea of it being Tremere himself who orchestrated it as Goratrix, but Karl Schreckt seems like it could be a possiblity. Although, it makes a lot more sense if it were Tremere, since he'd have an easier time blinding them to the incoming strike. It seems odd that a clan with Auspex as an in clan discipline could have their headquarters taken by surprise. I strongly suspect/hope that a lot more of clan leadership will come out of the woodwork. I do really dig House Carna incorporating other styles of magic, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T06:01:53-07:00","id":1401330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1248937-v5-vienna-tremere-friends?p=1401286#post1401286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it only makes sense if it were an inside job. I dig the idea of it being Tremere himself who orchestrated it as Goratrix, but Karl Schreckt seems like it could be a possiblity. Although, it makes a lot more sense if it were Tremere, since he'd have an easier time blinding them to the incoming strike. It seems odd that a clan with Auspex as an in clan discipline could have their headquarters taken by surprise. I strongly suspect/hope that a lot more of clan leadership will come out of the woodwork. I do really dig House Carna incorporating other styles of magic, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Premonition is not infallible, and BJD posits that the leadership is under the sway of the worm, so likely the strongest Kindred there would not have been in their right minds to deal with any accurate premonitions. Also, Premonition is going to give them some visuals related to what's happening but isn't going to be like CCTV or a movie of someone watching a drone from above. Likely the symbolism would've been there and those that saw it didn't have time to react. Assuming older vampires could interpret all the symbolism in such a modern method of war. It's not odd so much as it's unexplained so far (and likely purposely left open for STs to play with as they will, can you imagine the fun of a Tremere group sneaking into Fortschritt to try to recover stuff that might have survived the bombing?), and the great majority of WoD fans seem to crave explanations in detailed minutiae, and since V5 didn't do that in the core book (and god, that would add like 150 pages to do everything covered in the core book in broad strokes in minutiae).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T14:07:00-07:00","id":1401391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1248937-v5-vienna-tremere-friends?p=1401226#post1401226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One other theory about the Fall of Vienna and the inside job is that it was orchestrated by Karl Schreckt, who talked about issues with the SauloTremere worm and the control it had with the Council of Seven. And Schrekt was high up enough to know some of the ins and outs of everything.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26160\" data-vbnamecard=\"26160\">Koronus</a><br /> If she's that dedicated to Thaumaturgy itself, it's possible she actually jumped Anarch and went with the Ipsissimus. What we know about them fits her 'driven by Thaumaturgical development' and 'helping others'. The Ipsissimus Tremere are all about experimentation and advancement of magic in ways that were stifled by the Tremere hierarchy and methodology, and about doing it in tandem with each other. One of the quotes from the Ipsissimus in the Anarch book is We can all achieve enlightenment, but no-one should make that journey alone. It fits her concept probably the best, since Carna is about more specific neo-pagan witchcraft styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I got today the pre-order bonus of the preview pdf for the german Anarchs book and from what there is discripted is, that Ipsissimus is an inhuman house that would not care about the people they would kill for the research and are only at the anarchs to be sure to never be bound again. So I think it will be either Carna or Schreckt because for her, her human side and the love she can get with it with her love and her history would make her stay away from ritual sacrifices.<br /> Though it whas interessting, that House Schreckt tried to resettle Vienna and seems to plan an expedition for potential surviving artifacts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T15:03:23-07:00","id":1401396,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26160\" data-vbnamecard=\"26160\">Koronus</a> I think she should go with Carna. They would be the most sympathetic to her relationship with her boyfriend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T23:46:51-07:00","id":1401439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1248937-v5-vienna-tremere-friends?p=1401330#post1401330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Premonition is not infallible, and BJD posits that the leadership is under the sway of the worm, so likely the strongest Kindred there would not have been in their right minds to deal with any accurate premonitions. Also, Premonition is going to give them some visuals related to what's happening but isn't going to be like CCTV or a movie of someone watching a drone from above. Likely the symbolism would've been there and those that saw it didn't have time to react. Assuming older vampires could interpret all the symbolism in such a modern method of war. It's not odd so much as it's unexplained so far (and likely purposely left open for STs to play with as they will, can you imagine the fun of a Tremere group sneaking into Fortschritt to try to recover stuff that might have survived the bombing?), and the great majority of WoD fans seem to crave explanations in detailed minutiae, and since V5 didn't do that in the core book (and god, that would add like 150 pages to do everything covered in the core book in broad strokes in minutiae).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just the sheer amount of vampires that should have had high level Auspex still makes it seem very out of place it could have been taken by surprise without it being an inside job. It seems weird that at least more of the leadership couldn't have escaped even without a clear specific idea of what the threat was, especially with all the rituals they can use to escape. It might not be a specific knowledge of how it was going to happen, but imminent destruction was always a low difficulty roll and it's enough to know to flee. If Tremere or even the worm Saulot thing was working against them, it all makes perfect sense for them to be blinded. Maybe that's what the sacrifice of the antitribu was for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T02:21:26-07:00","id":1401447,"title":"","content":"Would there also be a case for those who got the premonitions, to have suffered a case of hubrises - &quot;Of course nothing can get through the wards and defences here&quot; - so even if warned didn't overly act. Though also pointing to the theory of an inside job. Also as a related tangent, aren't the actions of the Second Inquisition in London also possibly an inside job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T06:23:16-07:00","id":1401474,"title":"","content":"I should note the Society of Leopold isn't lacking in its own magicians. The Brethren of Albertus are not anywhere near the Council of Seven but they don't HAVE to be. All they have to be would be to make a small group blind enough long enough to let the place be bombed after a brief infiltration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T06:54:00-07:00","id":1401475,"title":"","content":"Lol this matter will never settle down.<br /> <br /> Just pay att. to the meta motive behind the writing and everything get clear.<br /> <br /> The developers want more Requiem, but Masquerade sell more. The solution was to do Requiem with masquerade make-up. This is why in v5 they get ride of Council of Seven, the majority of elders (but they try to sit in 2 horses in the same jump when they say every st will decide if same elders, fewer elders or no elders even if the book says no elders). This way the masquerade get more akin to Requiem with street level, local intrigue. Vianna Chantry was a obstacle because there have power play, elders, global conflict three things anti-requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","user":"blailton","date":". 07-07-2020, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"